  before reading any spec body.
outcomes:
  desired:
    - A no-path call returns a project-wide tree map with locations and type tags only — cheap enough to call speculatively at session start.
    - A path-scoped call opens with the ancestor chain (root to target, each carrying its description and any non-default status) before the subtree detail.
    - Misaligned specs surface inline in the chain so any agent walking the tree notices drift without a separate validation call.
